\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Two different time accounts. Top: for one fixed delay, causal observation reads earlier carrier data, while the finite-window temporal adjoint evaluates a later test time and has a prehistory part. Bottom: empty added states impose the proven latency bounds; the constant carrier-preload witness gives strict receiving and a nonzero incoming boundary trace on short open intervals. Interval lengths and positions are schematic. These are supports and bounds, not simulated waveforms or exact onset amplitudes.}}{20}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
